1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:14,000
Every year, Costco sells over 130 million hot dog and soda combos
And since 1985, the price hasn't budged a single cent: exactly one dollar and fifty cents

2
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:26,000
In this video, we'll uncover the secret unit economics behind the world's most famous loss leader — and why losing millions on lunch is actually Costco's single most brilliant profit engine.

3
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:44,000
To understand Costco, you have to realize one startling fact: Costco doesn't make money selling groceries
In a typical supermarket, products are marked up by 25 to 30 percent

4
00:00:44,000 --> 00:01:06,000
So where does Costco's profit come from? The answer lies in their SEC Form 10-K: Membership Fees
In 2023, Costco collected 4.6 billion dollars in membership dues, representing over 72 percent of total operating profit.

5
00:01:06,000 --> 00:01:22,000
Costco understood what Wall Street analysts often miss: when you build an ironclad covenant of value with your customer, they will happily pay you an annual subscription just for the privilege of walking through your doors
The hot dog isn't a sacrifice
